# Everything here is excluded from the build context.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` ships the virtualenv, the git history
# and every __pycache__ to the build daemon: slow builds, a bloated
# image, and a real risk of baking a local .env or database into a
# layer where it lives forever.

# Virtualenvs -- hundreds of MB, and platform-specific binaries that
# would be wrong inside the image anyway.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Python artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Test and tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local data. A development database copied into the image would be
# served to users of that image.
*.db
*.sqlite*
data/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Developer scripts with no role in the image.
#
# README.md is deliberately NOT listed here: pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so the build stage cannot produce a wheel
# without it. It costs a few KB in a stage that is discarded anyway,
# and excluding it breaks the build outright -- which is exactly what
# happened the first time this image was built.
Makefile
check.ps1
